index 34eb408..148f93e 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
-- Assert that a grandmaster change in WAITING enters DELAY with the zero to four second draw kind ([MFDISC-01](docs/REQUIREMENTS.md#mfdisc-01), Milan v1.2 5.6.3.5.7), and plant the startup kind at that call site, which the suite now catches ([milan-fpga #970](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/970), review finding R887-1-F1). No constant or behaviour changes.
+- Assert that a grandmaster change in WAITING enters DELAY with a fresh draw of the zero to four second kind ([MFDISC-01](docs/REQUIREMENTS.md#mfdisc-01), Milan v1.2 5.6.3.5.7), and plant two defects at that call site, the startup kind and a re-arm without a draw, which the suite now catches ([milan-fpga #970](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/970)). No constant or behaviour changes.
 - Walk only the sinks an ACMP entry changed. Each entry marks the sinks it changes, and its interface's timer for an expiry; completion and each publication before a new frame publish, re-arm, admit, persist and report only those, with the calls a walk over every sink makes, in its order and with its arguments ([ACMP-13](docs/REQUIREMENTS.md#acmp-changed-sink-walk)). Add `dirty`, `ACMP_DIRTY_WORDS` words, and `dirty_if` to `struct acmp`. A differential test drives random entries into a core and one with every sink marked before each entry, at 1, 8, 32 and 33 sinks, and requires the same calls. At 33 sinks its commands reach sink 32, alone on a third interface, and transmit room is withdrawn as at the other sizes. After each entry it requires every mark cleared.
 - Size the ACMP owed-release mask from `ACMP_MAX_SINKS`: `acmp_owed.release` holds `ACMP_RELEASE_WORDS` 32-bit words, and no shift reaches the word width. With more than 32 sinks, sink 32 and sink 0 no longer share a bit, so each sink's change waits only behind its own owed response. A build whose mask cannot hold every sink is refused, and so is a build of more than 255 sinks, which `probe_of` cannot name. Add a 33-sink test binary under `-fsanitize=shift,undefined`. It checks that sinks 31 and 32, on both sides of the word boundary, wait only behind their own owed responses, and that a probe owed in a slot that held another sink's response holds no sink. The 16-sink tests check the same slot reuse ([issue 31](https://github.com/kebag-logic/tsn-c-stack/issues/31)).
 - Exempt the merge of #29 from the one-line message rule by its exact commit; its identity and content are still checked.
